@startuml
title Refund a Failed Payment (US-19)

autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Customer\n(AppUser)" as Customer
participant "Biller\n(AquaCo)" as Biller <<external>>
participant "Payment" as Payment
participant "Wallet" as Wallet
participant "LedgerEntry" as Ledger
participant "AuditLog" as Audit
participant "Notification" as Notif

note over Payment, Wallet : Payment is SENT_TO_BILLER and its funds are held (352.50)

Biller -> Payment : refuses (error code)
Payment -> Payment : [SENT_TO_BILLER -> FAILED]\n(PaymentStateHistory saved)

Payment -> Wallet : releaseHold(payment)
Wallet -> Ledger : HOLD_RELEASE already exists for this payment?

alt yes (release triggered again)
    Ledger --> Wallet : yes
    Wallet --> Payment : ignored, no second refund\n(ledger has exactly one release entry)
else no (first release)
    Ledger --> Wallet : no
    Wallet -> Ledger : add HOLD_RELEASE entry\n(held -> available)
    Wallet -> Audit : record release (who, when, why, amount, payment ref)
    Wallet --> Payment : hold released
    Payment -> Payment : [FAILED -> REFUNDED]
    Payment -> Notif : payment failed + reason
    Notif --> Customer : SMS + push with a clear reason
end

note over Payment
    The same release path is used when an UNKNOWN payment
    is later resolved as FAILED (re-query says "not paid"
    or reconciliation finds no payment) - US-21, US-22.
end note

@enduml
